# CLAUDE.md

Guidance for Claude Code (and any other agent) working in this repository.

## What this repo is

Documentation, configuration, and knowledge capture for {{NAME}}.

It is **not** a software project: there is no build, no test suite, no linter. Changes are prose,
tables, checklists, and config files that get applied to a device by hand. "Correct" here means
accurate, sourced, and reproducible — not compiling.

## Build state (keep current)

As of {{DATE}}: <parts ordered / in transit / on the bench>. **Nothing in this repo has been
executed on the hardware** until the bring-up checklist says otherwise. Anything asserting device
behavior is sourced from vendor docs, upstream source, or community reports and carries a verify
marker.

Open blockers: see [`TODO.md`](TODO.md) and [`docs/accessories.md`](docs/accessories.md).

## Where things belong

| If it is… | It goes in |
|---|---|
| A hardware fact about a component | `hardware/specs/`, or `docs/reference/` for pin maps |
| A link to an upstream datasheet or schematic | `hardware/datasheets/README.md` |
| A repeatable procedure | `docs/runbooks/` |
| A pass/fail list run once at a milestone | `docs/checklists/` |
| Setup notes for one application | `software/<app>.md` |
| A file that gets copied onto the device | `configs/<subsystem>/` |
| A purchase, order, invoice, or warranty fact | `docs/records/` |
| Durable domain understanding | `knowledge/<discipline>/learned/` |
| A dated observation or capture | `knowledge/<discipline>/findings/` |
| A dated account of what was done | `docs/logs/build-log.md` |

Cross-link with **relative** links. Every document should be reachable from [`README.md`](README.md).

## Conventions

- **Verify markers.** Anything not confirmed on this hardware says so, in the sentence that makes
  the claim — "*unverified*", "verify before running", or a named command that settles it.
- **Estimates are labelled** and name the command whose output replaces them.
- **UTC timestamps.** Location recorded as city or grid square only — never precise coordinates.
- **No secrets.** No keys, PSKs, passwords, tokens, or captured credentials.
- **Binaries stay out.** Reference images and captures by location and checksum.
- **Commands are runnable.** State the expected output when it is the point of the step.
- **Tables over paragraphs**; checkbox lists for anything performed once. Markdown only.

## Living documents — update as a side effect of work

| File | Update when |
|---|---|
| [`docs/logs/build-log.md`](docs/logs/build-log.md) | Any hands-on session |
| [`docs/logs/known-issues.md`](docs/logs/known-issues.md) | A symptom is hit or resolved |
| [`docs/logs/decisions.md`](docs/logs/decisions.md) | A choice is made or a question closes |
| [`docs/logs/firmware-versions.md`](docs/logs/firmware-versions.md) | Anything is flashed |
| [`docs/records/order-and-warranty.md`](docs/records/order-and-warranty.md) | Shipping/serial/RMA changes |
| [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) / [`TODO.md`](TODO.md) | Work lands / a blocker appears |

## Checks before committing

```bash
python3 scripts/check_links.py    # no broken relative links
git status --short                # nothing unexpected staged
```

## Git

- Work on a feature branch; do not commit to the default branch directly.
- Commit messages: imperative subject, body explaining *why* the documentation changed and what is
  still unverified.
